      "created_at": "2026-10-28T23:23:44Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-28T23:23:44Z",
      "body": "Thanks for your PR @jpantonow, I took a look at the change and on Android, `SSLContext.getInstance(\"SSL\")` and `SSLContext.getInstance(\"TLS\")` resolve to the same implementation. Conscrypt registers \"SSL\" as an alias of \"TLS\" (https://github.com/google/conscrypt/blob/5bdcae0fe8aeb92009eba087969aed7f0ae0e167/common/src/main/java/org/conscrypt/OpenSSLProvider.java#L92-L94), and the negotiated protocol version is set by OkHttp's `ConnectionSpec` on each connection rather than by this string.\r\n\r\nSo this change doesn't alter runtime behaviour; it only satisfies the CrySL `SSLContextSpec` rule. We'll hold off merging for now since it doesn't change anything functionally.",
      "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
      "reactions": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/session-foundation/session-android/issues/comments/6483326974/reactions",
