      "created_at": "2026-11-07T01:39:05Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-11-07T01:39:05Z",
      "body": "Thanks for checking this, and for the Conscrypt link. You're right: on Android \"SSL\" is an alias of \"TLS\", so this change doesn't alter what gets negotiated. The only effect is that the code then states the protocol it actually uses, which keeps checkers like RVSec quiet and avoids confusion for readers. If you'd rather not take a change that is only cosmetic, feel free to close it. No problem at all.",
